<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>SkellyForge · Recording comparison</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="recording_comparison.css"></head><body>
<header><div><span class="eyebrow">SKELLYFORGE / RECORDING REVIEW</span><h1>Compare the fits</h1></div><div class="header-actions"><span id="recording-name"></span><a href="solver_viewer.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open solver lab ↗</a></div></header>
<main><section id="media-workspace"><section id="video-panel"><div class="section-title"><h2>Annotated recording</h2><label class="muted"><input type="checkbox" id="show-video" checked> Show</label></div><select id="camera" aria-label="Annotated camera"></select><div id="video-box"><img id="video-image" alt="Annotated recording frame" hidden><span id="video-placeholder">Loading matched frame…</span></div><div id="video-status" class="muted" aria-live="polite"></div></section>
<div id="video-divider" class="divider vertical" role="separator" aria-label="Resize annotated video width" aria-orientation="vertical" tabindex="0"></div>
<section id="viewport" aria-label="3D recording comparison"><div id="scene-toolbar"><button id="reset-camera">Reset camera</button><label>Focus <select id="region"><option value="all">Whole body</option><option>Trunk</option><option>Left arm</option><option>Right arm</option><option>Head and neck</option><option>Left hand</option><option>Right hand</option><option>Left leg and foot</option><option>Right leg and foot</option></select></label><span id="active-count"></span></div><div id="scene"></div><div id="overlay-legend"></div><div id="scene-hint">Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom · Right-drag to pan · Hover for identities</div><div id="tooltip" hidden></div></section>
</section>
<div id="sidebar-divider" class="divider vertical" role="separator" aria-label="Resize review sidebar" aria-orientation="vertical" tabindex="0"></div>
<aside><section id="controls"><div class="section-title"><h2>Saved fit inventory</h2><div><button id="hide-all">Hide all</button> <button id="reset-solutions">Reset comparison</button></div></div><p id="inventory-summary" class="muted"></p><p class="table-help">Check to overlay. Display: color and opacity (%). Solo isolates a fit; Details inspects it.</p><div id="solutions" class="table-scroll"></div>
<details id="fit-inspector"><summary>Inspect: <span id="inspector-title"></span></summary><p id="inspector-warning" class="frame-warning"></p><p id="inspector-objective"></p><dl id="inspector-facts" class="audit-facts"></dl><details><summary>Saved metrics and Ceres report</summary><dl id="inspector-metrics" class="audit-facts"></dl><pre id="inspector-report"></pre></details><details><summary>Exact saved solver settings</summary><pre id="inspector-settings"></pre></details></details>
<details open><summary>Reference & geometry layers</summary><div class="layers"><label><input id="show-keypoints" type="checkbox" checked> Keypoints · cyan solid spheres</label><label><input id="show-landmarks" type="checkbox" checked> Fitted landmarks · solution-colored wire spheres</label><label><input id="show-segments" type="checkbox" checked> Fitted segments</label><label><input id="show-linkages" type="checkbox" checked> Relaxed shoulder connectors</label><label><input id="show-saved-landmarks" type="checkbox"> Saved posthoc landmarks · gray wire spheres</label><label><input id="show-saved-segments" type="checkbox"> Saved posthoc segments · gray sticks</label><label><input id="show-axes" type="checkbox"> Local XYZ axes and labeled origins</label><label><input id="show-grid" type="checkbox" checked> Ground grid</label></div></details>
<details><summary>How to compare</summary><p>All enabled fits share the same recording frame and world coordinates. No alignment, scaling, or fitting happens in this viewer. Fitted landmarks are model points; cyan keypoints are tracker measurements.</p><p>Bone thickness tapers toward the distal end. Short shoulder connectors show fitted attachment separation, not bone length changes. Hover to inspect identities and coordinates. Opacity and body focus affect display only.</p><p>Saved posthoc layers are reference context, not another Ceres fit. A small target error or convergence does not establish anatomical accuracy.</p></details></section>
</aside></main>
<footer><div class="timeline-labels"><span id="start-label"></span><output id="frame-label"></output><span id="end-label"></span></div><input id="timeline" type="range" min="0" value="0" step="1" aria-label="Recording timeline"><div class="transport"><div><button id="first" aria-label="First frame">|◀</button><button id="previous" aria-label="Previous frame">◀</button><button id="play" class="primary">Play</button><button id="next" aria-label="Next frame">▶</button><button id="last" aria-label="Last frame">▶|</button></div><div><label><input id="loop" type="checkbox" checked> Loop</label><label>Speed <select id="speed"><option value="0.25">¼×</option><option value="0.5">½×</option><option value="1" selected>1×</option><option value="2">2×</option></select></label><label>Frame <input id="frame-number" type="number" step="1"></label><span class="muted">Space: play/pause · ← →: step</span></div></div></footer>
<script>const RECORDING_COMPARISON=__DATA__;</script><script src="vendor/three.min.js"></script><script src="vendor/OrbitControls.js"></script><script src="recording_comparison_scene.js"></script><script src="recording_comparison_table.js"></script><script src="recording_comparison.js"></script></body></html>
